New finding (MED, logged, non-blocking):
`j6_site_universe.py:796-810` — sharded runs have **no completeness gate**. `expected_shards` written but never read back; `--check-smn-anchors` forbidden when `shard_count != 1`, so the array path has no acceptance check. Probed: `--shard-count 2 --shard-index 0` exits 0 with `expected 2 committed 1` — a preempted task leaves a silently partial directory whose `*.done` glob all validates. Fix: `verify_run_complete(output_dir)` requiring every expected shard to have a validated `.done` with matching `run_sha256`. Not blocking because no J6 consumer exists yet (grepped).

